Third-party code and data
-------------------------

Code or data adapted from other open-source projects is listed here, with its
licence and the files it appears in.

- internal/agents/rules/*.toml: screen-rule patterns adapted from Herdr's agent
  detection manifests (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr, src/detect/manifests),
  Copyright the Herdr authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  The rule format and engine are our own; the patterns were simplified.

- vt/src/snapshot.zig: the approach to serialising terminal state is adapted
  from zmx's serializeTerminalState (https://github.com/neurosnap/zmx,
  src/util.zig), Copyright (c) 2025 Eric Bower, licensed under the MIT License.
  The full notice is in the file's header.
- vt/: links libghostty-vt from Ghostty (https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty),
  Copyright Mitchell Hashimoto and contributors, licensed under the MIT License.

The docs site (site/) ships these, unchanged or cut down by scripts/site-vendor.sh:
- site/assets/vendor/three/: three.js 0.186.1 (https://threejs.org),
  Copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors, licensed under the MIT License.
- site/static/fonts/mono.woff2: JetBrains Mono 2.304
  (https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono), Copyright 2020 The JetBrains
  Mono Project Authors, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- site/static/fonts/sans.woff2: Inter 4 (https://github.com/rsms/inter),
  Copyright 2016 The Inter Project Authors, licensed under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1.

Projects whose designs informed this one:
- zmx (https://github.com/neurosnap/zmx), MIT (and the code above)
- Herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr), Apache-2.0 (and the rule data above)

- internal/nettarget/wildcard_psl_data.go: negative ancestor data derived from
  the Public Suffix List, revision d6c92f1bbb7433e5db7b8405c25d4035fb8ff376
  (https://github.com/publicsuffix/list), licensed under MPL 2.0.
  The complete licence is in LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt. The pinned x/net library
  handles public suffix matching. The ancestor index adds only negative boundaries.

- internal/egress/rules/minted.json: three finite credential-family patterns
  derived from gitleaks v8.30.1, commit 83d9cd684c87d95d656c1458ef04895a7f1cbd8e
  (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/blob/83d9cd684c87d95d656c1458ef04895a7f1cbd8e/config/gitleaks.toml).
  This is a derived network-response subset. File and line allowlists,
  ignore comments and entropy suppression do not exempt response values.
  The complete upstream MIT copyright and permission notice follows.

